{"applicability":"Interpreting an obligation, selecting an assertion, or relying on checker soundness, completeness, observation sufficiency or reported test results.","argument":{"clause_arguments":[],"conditional_consequence":"Insufficient assertion strength or observations cannot support the broader required conclusion; favourable runs do not prove universal soundness.","policy_choices":["The source owner selects required meaning. The evaluation binding selects justified scope and instrumentation; probability and computational feasibility need further models."],"premises":[{"id":"F1","kind":"foundational_premise","owner":"FOUNDATIONS.foundational-commitments"},{"id":"F2","kind":"foundational_premise","owner":"FOUNDATIONS.foundational-commitments"},{"id":"F3","kind":"foundational_premise","owner":"FOUNDATIONS.foundational-commitments"},{"id":"F6","kind":"foundational_premise","owner":"FOUNDATIONS.foundational-commitments"}],"source_family_arguments":[{"additional_policy_and_owner":"The source owner fixes required meaning; the evaluation binding chooses its scope and instrumentation and supports actual conformance. A narrower scope needs justification; probability and computational feasibility require further models.","conditional_consequence":"A necessary-condition pass cannot establish a sufficient conclusion. Indistinguishable cases with different truth defeat a sound complete decision from that observation alone; favourable runs cannot establish universal checker soundness.","declared_consumer_scope":"[Assertions and observations](#assertions-and-observations), applied by Evaluate, testing oracles and acquired views","family":"[Assertions and observations](#assertions-and-observations), applied by Evaluate, testing oracles and acquired views","premise_and_pillar_argument":"F1 selects the source obligation; F2 binds interpretation and assertions; F3 binds observations; F6 limits conclusions to support. The instance supplies the case domain, observation map and checker relation. Information and evidence contribute the distinctions needed to judge the predicate.","premises":["F1","F2","F3","F6"],"required_when":"Only when assessing this family argument, its applicability, consequence, conservation, coverage or fidelity against this consumer. This is not an unconditional operational dependency.","source_refs":[{"anchor":"core-contract-derivations","path":"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md","required_when":"Only when assessing this family argument, its applicability, consequence, conservation, coverage or fidelity against this consumer. This is not an unconditional operational dependency.","role":"provenance"}],"source_row":{"anchor":"core-contract-derivations","hash_boundary":"Exact Markdown row including terminal newline.","line":1046,"path":"standards/FOUNDATIONS.md","sha256":"6fed7eab4740dc31694b180a9c4e692f8b2b9eb95740510cf6edcc2b7328f62a"}}],"source_refs":["FOUNDATIONS.assertions-and-observations","FOUNDATIONS.foundational-commitments"]},"definition":{"clauses":[{"Q_r":"interpret(r, Gamma, Omega), the required predicate preserving the obligation's scope.","q_t":"Assertion target predicate."},{"necessary":"Q_r implies q_t","sufficient":"q_t implies Q_r","sufficient_conjunction":"(q_1 and ... and q_n) implies Q_r"},{"R":"Existing core result records","T":"Admitted evaluation relation contained in O x R","pi":"Omega -> O, available-observation model","sat_fal":"Abbreviations for core verdicts on q_t, not execution states."},{"sound_falsification":"For every s: (pi(s),fal) in T implies not q_t(s)","sound_satisfaction":"For every s: (pi(s),sat) in T implies q_t(s)"},{"observation_sufficiency":"For all s,s' in Omega: pi(s)=pi(s') implies q_t(s)=q_t(s')"}],"kind":"supporting_definitions","structures":{}},"dependencies":["FOUNDATIONS.interpretation-and-representation","FOUNDATIONS.premises-and-standing","FOUNDATIONS.foundational-commitments","FOUNDATIONS.result-algebra"],"dependency_relations":[{"binding":"Retain source-to-predicate meaning.","id":"FOUNDATIONS.interpretation-and-representation","kind":"contract_application","required_when":"within the declared applicability"},{"binding":"Selected methodology scope and source-owned authority.","id":"FOUNDATIONS.premises-and-standing","kind":"contract_application","required_when":"within the declared applicability"},{"binding":"Only the named premise subset supports the conditional argument.","id":"FOUNDATIONS.foundational-commitments","kind":"contract_application","required_when":"within the declared applicability"},{"binding":"Preserve verdict, evaluation performance, original domain outcome and material effects.","id":"FOUNDATIONS.result-algebra","kind":"contract_application","required_when":"within the declared applicability"}],"id":"FOUNDATIONS.assertions-and-observations","inputs":[],"obligations":["Interpret the owning obligation on declared assumptions and cases including material inputs, behaviour and environment, preserving conditions, exceptions and alternatives. Text identity alone proves no interpretation fidelity.","State whether the assertion targets the full obligation or a narrower condition, and justify the implication relied on. A necessary-condition pass cannot establish the full obligation; a sufficient conjunction needs coverage and compatibility.","An equality oracle is justified only where the obligation requires equal outputs; different outputs may satisfy the same acceptable relation.","For every admitted case, a satisfied checker verdict implies the asserted predicate and a falsified verdict implies its negation, wherever those soundness directions are claimed. Retain unresolved support.","Universal soundness covers every admitted conclusion, not a favourable selected run. Actual checker and observation acquisition need conformance support; a selected model or ideal observation map does not supply it.","A reported pass or failure remains observation until oracle and observation justification support the claimed conclusion. Preserve original predicate, actual performance, uncertain effects and independently admissible counterevidence through the core.","A checker that always decides correctly from pi alone requires equal observations to imply equal predicate truth. A collision requires distinguishing evidence, justified narrower scope or indeterminate on that attempted decision."],"permissions_exceptions":["Human/probabilistic checkers may admit both a sound satisfied result and indeterminate. Deterministic checking is a scoped special case; the relation supplies no probability distribution.","In a classical set model observation sufficiency permits a predicate on pi's image, but supplies no executable procedure or cost bound."],"predicate":"The claimed assertion conclusion faithfully relates to its source obligation and is supported by the admitted checker and actual observation basis on its declared domain.","representation_kind":"constraint","result_mapping":{"conditions":"Evaluate this exact predicate and its scoped required conditions; retain all qualified domain outcomes, actual evaluation performance, material effect observations, and absent coverage.","contract_ref":"core.shared_contracts.core_evaluation","evaluation_contract_ref":"core.shared_contracts.core_evaluation","kind":"constraint_assessment","owner_refs":["FOUNDATIONS.result-algebra","FOUNDATIONS.result-conjunction"],"rules":[]},"scope_refs":["FOUNDATIONS.premises-and-standing"],"source_clause_ids":["FOUNDATIONS.assertions-and-observations#c1","FOUNDATIONS.assertions-and-observations#c2","FOUNDATIONS.assertions-and-observations#c3","FOUNDATIONS.assertions-and-observations#c4","FOUNDATIONS.assertions-and-observations#c5","FOUNDATIONS.assertions-and-observations#c6","FOUNDATIONS.assertions-and-observations#c7","FOUNDATIONS.assertions-and-observations#c8","FOUNDATIONS.assertions-and-observations#c9","FOUNDATIONS.assertions-and-observations#c10","FOUNDATIONS.assertions-and-observations#c11"],"source_clause_roles":[{"repres