{"applicability":"Adopted premises for selected STDO purposeful construction; other domains keep their declared dependencies.","argument":{"conditional_consequence":"Adopting the six distinct commitments supplies conditional premises for the method; it does not prove instance satisfaction or choose authority.","policy_choices":["The Product authority adopts F1-F6 and the selected methodology domain; additional domain policy remains separately owned."],"premises":[{"binding":"Use X,Y,K,P,I,G to explain selected operation adequacy, identity/support and actual grants without imposing a serialized schema.","id":"TRANSFORMATION_LIBRARY.foundational-contract","kind":"contract_application"}],"source_explanation":"A selected predicate, persistent workspace, material join or required independent assessment is an instance condition only when the bound contract supplies it. Finite capacity alone supplies none of them.","source_refs":["FOUNDATIONS.foundational-commitments"]},"definition":{"meaning":"F1 adopts selected outcome/adequacy with owner value choices; F2 interprets claims on exact subject/basis and leaves unsupported interpretation unresolved; F3 uses scoped identity and observable persistent state distinct from representation/history; F4 conserves material outer relations under declared compatibility/loss; F5 finite resources admit truthful handling of unknown/inadequate/interrupted states; F6 evidence supports claims while operation/decision grants retain their owners."},"dependencies":["TRANSFORMATION_LIBRARY.foundational-contract"],"dependency_relations":[{"binding":"Use X,Y,K,P,I,G to explain selected operation adequacy, identity/support and actual grants without imposing a serialized schema.","id":"TRANSFORMATION_LIBRARY.foundational-contract","kind":"contract_application"}],"id":"FOUNDATIONS.foundational-commitments","inputs":[],"obligations":["Material instance bindings explain adequate result, subject/interpretation, state/relations preserved, admitted unknown outcomes and authorized effects/dispositions.","A specialization adds types/predicates/policy/adoption without discarding selected generic guarantees; each deciding family must expose premises, consequence and independent choices, otherwise its specialization argument is unsupported.","Distinguish adopted commitments from instance premises supplied by the selected contract. Bind each family argument to its deciding owner, actual consumer and additional policy. Pillar contributions are explanatory contributions, not extra axioms or grants."],"permissions_exceptions":["These are adopted domain commitments, not theorems from finite capacity. They require no purpose field or mandatory record on every calculus entity; only material bindings apply. Total handling promises neither omniscience nor universal idempotence/termination/solution.","An argument owns no second version of its linked law and requires no additional work record."],"predicate":null,"representation_kind":"definition_data","result_mapping":{"contract_ref":"core.shared_contracts.definition_data","embedded_constraints":["Material instance bindings explain adequate result, subject/interpretation, state/relations preserved, admitted unknown outcomes and authorized effects/dispositions.","A specialization adds types/predicates/policy/adoption without discarding selected generic guarantees; each deciding family must expose premises, consequence and independent choices, otherwise its specialization argument is unsupported."],"kind":"domain_definition_or_data","predicate_binding":null},"scope_refs":["FOUNDATIONS.premises-and-standing"],"source_clauses":[{"byte_end":3489,"byte_start":3267,"id":"c1","roles":["scope","argument"],"sha256":"e77d9d48a90b8df514f80c5383d6eb4e7a998ce387e46ddf0d1d3a80ca718b22"},{"byte_end":4823,"byte_start":3491,"id":"c2","roles":["scope","argument"],"sha256":"ab94d2a5c8536a660713f74bd7154996e820b2b4065fa8176ae2a7016831623d"},{"byte_end":5450,"byte_start":4825,"id":"c3","roles":["obligation","argument"],"sha256":"3c2bcad6c90db6503c7f9615aff3cb1d5b3da19d37343f3aee2846f2f2ecf051"},{"byte_end":5950,"byte_start":5452,"id":"c4","roles":["argument"],"sha256":"ec7ad3ccf49af454623f35e01553cee90e057698c9ee6793d98a7a24b3089331"},{"byte_end":6641,"byte_start":3239,"id":"body","roles":["source_owned_body"],"sha256":"e63d38cbbad66411ce0762c790a360c6affb91612fecf1a8f4d9ffcf7965e947"}],"source_references":["TRANSFORMATION_LIBRARY.foundational-contract","TRANSFORMATION_LIBRARY.workrecovery-specialization"]}
